Notes on the possibility of a moral law

    - it was past credence in a divine creator that instilled our present sense of morality,
      an age-old consensus that dissolved and left intact a deontic sense of right behaviour
      informed by a concept of moral law
        : ad `our` : the West’s
    - now seeing our past credence justified (ex hypothesi) by new evidence, I consider whether the same
      evidence justifies also a [renewed|{renewal of}] belief in the reality of moral law
        : re `(credence) (justified).+by new evidence` cf. `${1} would be ${2}$` @
          `^*\(14b\) a design explanans is credible` @ 20.boneyard.brec
    - that {reality} would require|comprise meeting the conditions implied in the concept
        (-) conditions that suffice for [the realization of] a {divinity-based} moral law are:
